  "method": "As for 21299-shell-tapered-box-with-rounded-corners-and-loop: every round (R36, R10) is at least the 1 mm wall, so with T the drafted box (half-widths 65 - z/5 and 85 - z/5, 0 <= z <= 50), P = T without its top and bottom with the walls pushed in by 36, Pi = P + 26B and G = Pi n {z <= 40}: the body is K = (G + 10B) n {z >= 0} and the cavity C = (G + 9B) n {z >= 0} (walls in by 1, rounds 35 and 9, top at 49). A section of G + sB at z <= 40 is the rectangle of the walls pushed in by 10 - s with four corners cut by the ellipse of the inclined corner cylinder of radius 26 + s (semi-axes Rl along the diagonal and R across, l = sqrt(1 + 2 tan^2 a), tan a = 1/5): area 4AB - 4D, D = c(c - y1) - R^2 l atan(1/l), c = R sqrt((l^2+1)/2), y1 = R (l^2-1)/sqrt(2(l^2+1)), integrated in closed form. Above z = 40 the section is the set within s of G, its boundary found in each direction from the exact distance to G, integrated over z = 40 + s sin(phi) by Gauss-Legendre (64 points). With no draft the same code gives the closed form by Pappus to 7e-13. V(K) = 903166.6532 (SolidCraft's measure of the body before the shell: 903166.6532, 4e-11), V(C) = 863804.6227, V = 39362.0305 mm3 (16, 32 and 64 points: .0330, .0303, .0305; 32000 directions as 8000). Faces: the body's 18 less the bottom, their 17 inner copies and the bottom's rim, 35",
